 "_doc": "Planned look of every city person (wave 2b), applied by tools/bodies/metahuman/make_bodies.py once MetaHuman Creator Core Data is installed. Wardrobe ids are not knowable before Core Data exists: each slot lists exact wardrobe item names to try first ('items', WI_* asset names under /MetaHumanCharacter/Optional/...), then 'keywords' (all must appear in the item name, case-insensitive; best partial match otherwise). Hair colour uses the groom pipeline's parameters: melanin 0 (blond) .. 1 (black), redness 0..1, whiteness 0..1 (grey/white), lightness 0..1. Skin: u ~ melanin (0 light .. 1 dark), v ~ undertone (0 cool/pink .. 1 warm/yellow), on MetaHuman Creator's skin-tone picker. face_texture_index picks the synthesized skin detail set (pores, wrinkles); its ordering by age is unknown until Core Data exists, so it is a starting value to tune after the first render. Outfit 'colors' are matched against the outfit's instance parameters by name (e.g. PrimaryColorShirt). Low (far) bodies get the same choices; the assembly turns hair into cards/helmets and the server never shows strands on Low. Setting: a solarpunk village, everyday practical clothes (linen, knit, canvas, aprons, work trousers), muted natural dyes.",
